cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or its results, please cite it as below."
title: "Plant-based diet quality and cardiometabolic dysfunction in US adults: a reproducible survey-weighted analysis of NHANES 2017-March 2020"
abstract: >-
  A fully reproducible, survey-weighted, cross-sectional analysis of plant-based
  diet quality (PDI/hPDI/uPDI) and cardiometabolic dysfunction among US adults,
  using NHANES 2017-March 2020 pre-pandemic data and USDA FPED/FNDDS. The
  analysis combines isocaloric food-group substitution modelling within the
  plant-based diet index framework with regression calibration for within-person
  24-hour recall measurement error. The study is observational; all estimates are
  associations and no causal claims are made.
type: software
